{"resourceIdentifier":"1414","resourceName":"Sustainable Climate-Friendly Coffee (CO2 Coffee)","description":"This project involves the participation of coffee producers who have obtained Rainforest Alliance certification, which is based on compliance with the Sustainable Agriculture Network standard. The project proponent seeks to quantify the climate mitigation benefits generated through the implementation of more environmentally sustainable land use practices using the criteria of the Verified Carbon Standard (VCS). The overall objective of the project is to enhance and quantify the GHG removals of additional tree cover in areas of certified coffee production (“cafetales”), as well as surrounding areas in the landscape previously degraded by cattle and shifting agriculture (“potreros” and “acahuales”). The project uses native trees adapted to the region with the aim of enhancing forest carbon stocks in eligible areas over a period of 30 years, while promoting sustainable coffee production and contributing to reducing the agricultural frontier.","location":{"latitude":16.140370,"longitude":-97.188288},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1414"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Oaxaca"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Late to verify"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4337"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ARR"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AR-AM0007"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"292 Hectares"}]},{"co